# B4 on the blocked BACK/LEFT/RIGHT episodes: who gets out of whose way?

Deterministic replay. The *blocking car* is the nearest car between ego and the slot, in the slot's
lane, at reset. It *leaves* when it starts a lane change of its own (its MOBIL model decides this;
the anchor never changes lane, other cars may). Ego *passes it in its lane* when ego gets ahead of it
while it is still in its starting lane.

## B4_seed7

| Blocking car | Episodes | Reached | Crashed into it | Crashed into another car | Timeout |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| stays in its lane | 18 | 3 | 15 | 0 | 0 |
| leaves its lane by itself | 27 | 21 | 2 | 4 | 0 |

- Ego passed a blocking car that was still in its lane: 0/45 episodes.
- Slot in ego's own lane (27 episodes): ego started a lane change while behind the blocking car in 1, and chose SLOWER while behind it in 0.
- Reached although the blocking car stayed: [10071, 10082, 10158].
- The 17 crashes into the blocking car. Critic value (shaping removed; a crash is -150): -13.5 at reset, -12.5 at the last decision, 0.1 s before the crash (3 of them above 0).
- Same crashes, sampling probabilities per decision while behind the blocking car (what training explores): LANE_LEFT 1.9%, IDLE 54.4%, LANE_RIGHT 14.3%, FASTER 22.6%, SLOWER 6.8%.

